&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About X:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is Alphabet’s moonshot factory with a mission of inventing and launching moonshot technologies that could someday make the world a radically better place. We are a diverse group of inventors and entrepreneurs who build and launch technologies that aim to improve the lives of millions, even billions, of people. Our goal: 10x impact on the world’s most intractable problems, not just 10% improvement. We approach projects that have the aspiration and riskiness of research with the speed and ambition of a startup. As an innovation engine, X focuses on repeatedly turning breakthrough-technology ideas into the foundations for large, sustainable businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an extraordinary, multi-talented scientist/engineer to join a core effort in X’s BioDesign Kitchen to help accelerate moonshots in biology and chemistry. This is a hands-on role to help shape our interface of frontier models with the physical practice of the scientific discipline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t a traditional siloed role. You are a rare hybrid who understands scientific processes and the instruments that make them possible, while appreciating the messy complexity of biological systems. As a core member of our team, you will be the bridge between the digital, physical, and cellular worlds—owning the design and execution of intelligent closed-loop systems that automate, analyze, and accelerate biological discovery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is in the BioDK and is core to its mission of rapidly prototyping moonshots in chemistry and biology. This position will directly serve existing and future moonshots in the BioDK, and help in the creation and co-creation of new moonshots, and advance our AI4Science efforts. The role will also involve efficient communication of results, concepts, and progress.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10x impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge the Domains:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary technical nexus between our Machine Learning, Hardware, Biology, and Chemistry teams, translating complex experimental constraints into algorithmic and hardware requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Closed-Loop Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, build, and deploy end-to-end automated laboratory workflows where AI-driven models control physical hardware/robotics to execute and iterate on biological experiments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware-Software Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop custom firmware, APIs, or drivers to connect proprietary laboratory automation hardware with cloud-based AI infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Pipeline &amp;amp; Protocol Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Design robust data engineering pipelines to capture, clean, and structure messy, high-throughput biological data (e.g., genomic, proteomic, or imaging data) for ML training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Independently scope, prototype, and test high-risk technical features, moving rapidly from ambiguous ideas to concrete, working physical prototypes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Ph.D. in and strong research track record in Biophyisics, Chemistry, Biology, Bioengineering, Chemical Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years of professional or postdoc experience working directly at the intersection of biology, hardware, and software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with hardware prototyping, sensor integration, microcontrollers (e.g., Arduino, ESP32, Raspberry Pi), and protocols (SPI, I2C, UART). You should be comfortable with the insides of a computer, and be able to tell SATA from serial connections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimental:&lt;/strong&gt; High level of proficiency in a wet lab environment; deep understanding of molecular biology, assay development, cell or tissue culture, synthetic biology. Protein engineering experience a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong proficiency in python, the use of agent harnesses, and github.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; you will be astute at communicating deeply technical ideas in a straightforward way to non-expert colleagues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also have these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with laboratory automation standards and frameworks (e.g., pylabrobot or Hamilton, Tecan, Agilent Bravo).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An intense curiosity to learn new techniques and work with colleagues with complementary skill sets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Protein engineering experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mechanical aptitude&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A thrive-in-chaos mentality: Comfort with extreme ambiguity, rapid pivoting, and a passion for tackling 10x problems rather than 10% improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $132,000 - $195,000 + bonus + benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tapestry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tapestry is a group within Google working to build the AI-powered electric grid. We are tackling one of the world’s most important infrastructure challenges: helping the energy system become more visible, understandable, reliable, affordable, abundant, and clean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Originally born at X, Alphabet’s moonshot factory, Tapestry brings together experts in energy, AI, software engineering, and products to build tools that help the electricity ecosystem plan smarter, move faster, and operate more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global effort. Tapestry supports partners across the U.S., U.K., Chile, New Zealand, Australia, and Brazil as they work toward a cleaner, more resilient energy future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Tapestry means doing high-impact work with a multidisciplinary team tackling a problem that matters at global scale. Learn more about our team and our mission &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tapestryenergy.com/en&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Business Development Lead at Tapestry, you will be responsible for identifying, prioritizing, and advancing strategic commercial and partnership opportunities across global energy markets. The position will work directly with energy industry participants including developers, utilities, and grid operators. This role will increase new business velocity, but is&amp;nbsp; not a traditional quota-carrying sales position. A Business Development Lead at Tapestry will focus on accelerating commercial opportunities through strategic, innovative business development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with product, power systems engineers, partnerships and leadership to understand customer needs, validate use cases, and structure early commercial and partnership engagements. The ideal candidate is comfortable operating in ambiguity, balancing long-term opportunity development with near-term execution, and helping define how business development works at an early-stage company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10X Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, qualify, prioritize, and advance strategic partnership and early commercial opportunities aligned with Tapestry’s product roadmap and technical capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and lead partnership discussions with utilities, energy providers, and ecosystem partners, including framing Tapestry&#39;s product value and impact, defining mutual success criteria, and establishing clear commercial terms and expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with product, engineering, and leadership to translate market signals into product direction and development priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with industry stakeholders to understand regulatory dynamics, market trends, and competitive landscapes across global energy markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design and execution of early commercial engagements,&amp;nbsp; including non-standard partnership structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and communicate opportunity progress and learnings, providing regular updates that inform strategy and support company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Tapestry externally at industry events and partner forums to build credibility, relationships, and long-term market presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant experience in the energy or electricity industry, preferably in business development, partnerships, or commercial strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with utilities, energy providers, grid operators, or adjacent ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead complex, multi-stakeholder discussions in ambiguous or early-stage environments, including rigorous attention to detail, stakeholder management, and follow through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to personally structure and execute the financial logic, deal economics, and understand required commercial terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to build relationships and influence across technical, commercial, and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and negotiating non-standard commercial agreements,or innovative partnership structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to clearly synthesize and share insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Salesforce or similar CRM tools for opportunity tracking and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had one or more of&amp;nbsp; these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with power systems, grid operations, or energy market structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or launching early-stage or first-of-kind products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in fast-paced environments with evolving priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical thinking and ability to articulate trade-offs and implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial mindset with a collaborative, low-ego approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take charge&lt;/strong&gt;: We take initiative and own outcomes that move the mission forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transform with purpose: &lt;/strong&gt;We build solutions that solve real problems and create meaningful impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Tapestry, not a thread&lt;/strong&gt;: We collaborate across diverse skills and perspectives to achieve more than we can individually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always fine-tune&lt;/strong&gt;: We stay curious, seek feedback, and refine our understanding as we learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay grounded:&lt;/strong&gt; We listen openly, value different perspectives, and stay focused on what matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A culture that supports growth, ownership, and meaningful impact, along with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and flexible hybrid work model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work on important real-world problems within an Alphabet-backed environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $168,000 - $246,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About X:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is Alphabet’s moonshot factory with a mission of inventing and launching moonshot technologies that could someday make the world a radically better place. We are a diverse group of inventors and entrepreneurs who build and launch technologies that aim to improve the lives of millions, even billions, of people. Our goal: 10x impact on the world’s most intractable problems, not just 10% improvement. We approach projects that have the aspiration and riskiness of research with the speed and ambition of a startup. As an innovation engine, X focuses on repeatedly turning breakthrough-technology ideas into the foundations for large, sustainable businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This senior role sits within the critical Business Innovation team at X. We partner and embed with our deep-tech project teams to accelerate and transform our moonshots from the earliest and riskiest stages into de-risked, investable ventures. We work with our moonshot projects to build and iterate on their moonshot investment theses, setting the holistic business foundations for successful moonshots. We prove and build our path to the moon through early contact with the real world across market and ecosystem validation, business model and GTM iterative de-risking, product creation, investment readiness, and internal and external partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking experienced business innovators with deep expertise in business building and commercialisation who are motivated by a passion to change the world for the better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role seeks motivated individuals that enjoy working in small, interdisciplinary teams, have a growth mindset, a passion for problem-solving directed at achieving meaningful business and commercial breakthroughs, and are comfortable with uncertainty, exploration, and iteration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Business Innovation team member, you will work closely with several cross-disciplinary teams across the factory, Alphabet and external partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10x impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead market, business, product and partnerships strategy for specific moonshot projects including diving into exciting experiments and shaping key strategic initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Roll up your sleeves on projects as an embedded Business Innovation team member with radical collaboration to accelerate our moonshots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply first principles systems thinking with the ability to set hypotheses and test them in the market with stakeholders and partners to progressively de-risk moonshot projects from a business perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As ‘player-coaches’, show up as critical thought partners and co-builders with our project leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the investment readiness process for internal ventures preparing to graduate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage our convening power and resources at X and Alphabet in your pursuit of accelerating moonshots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 years of professional business experience with a significant focus on deep tech either through entrepreneurship, investing, management consulting or operating in a technical industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset with a strong propensity to learn and innovate through proactive problem, market, customer discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep analytical rigour, including demonstrable expertise with financial modelling for market, business and product development strategy. Specifically, deep experience and comfort with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market discovery and analysis including stakeholder/expert interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product marketing analysis (e.g. identifying and translating current unmet needs to moonshot product requirements, identifying target customer/user segments, revenue models and pricing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go-to-market strategy and sequencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business financial modeling (e.g. market sizing, unit economics, pro forma P&amp;amp;Ls)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create significant strategic partnerships around early stage technology or ventures including sourcing, building alignment and closing strategic partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of deep tech, emerging technologies, and the unique challenges of commercializing research and early technology innovations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional project management with a track record of successful, end-to-end project or deal execution, or entrepreneurial venture-building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills including ability to effectively communicate both technical and non-technical information to mixed audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively, lead through influence, and build strong relationships in a fast-paced, dynamic, and ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had these:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or equivalent strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to de-risk a new product idea from a business perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven entrepreneurial background with experience as a founder or as an early employee at an early-stage startup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience designing and executing go-to-market strategies for novel technology products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by purpose and passion; you fall in love with problems, not solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $180,000 - $277,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tapestry is a group within Google working to build the AI-powered electric grid. We are tackling one of the world’s most important infrastructure challenges: helping the energy system become more visible, understandable, reliable, affordable, abundant, and clean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Originally born at X, Alphabet’s moonshot factory, Tapestry brings together experts in energy, AI, software engineering, and products to build tools that help the electricity ecosystem plan smarter, move faster, and operate more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global effort. Tapestry supports partners across the U.S., U.K., Chile, New Zealand, Australia, and Brazil as they work toward a cleaner, more resilient energy future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Tapestry means doing high-impact work with a multidisciplinary team tackling a problem that matters at global scale. Learn more about our team and our mission here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a talented grid simulations and computational specialist to join Tapestry and help expand our high-performance grid computation capabilities. In this role, you will bridge power system physics with modern software architecture, designing simulation algorithms and optimization tools capable of handling complex, large-scale electrical networks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with a multidisciplinary team of AI researchers, software engineers, power systems domain experts, and product managers to turn complex technical challenges into production-ready solutions. By building advanced computational capabilities, you will empower global energy partners to accelerate the transition to clean energy, improve grid reliability, and unlock transformative 10x impact across the global energy ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make 10x impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with power system and software engineering experts on the design and creation of advanced simulation and optimization tools.&lt;/li&gt;
