&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About X:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is Alphabet’s moonshot factory with a mission of inventing and launching “moonshot” technologies that could someday make the world a radically better place. We are a diverse group of inventors and entrepreneurs who build and launch technologies that aim to improve the lives of millions, even billions, of people. Our goal: 10x impact on the world’s most intractable problems, not just 10% improvement. We approach projects that have the aspiration and riskiness of research with the speed and ambition of a startup. As an innovation engine, X focuses on repeatedly turning breakthrough-technology ideas into the foundations for large, sustainable businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Biological cells are the most sophisticated manufacturing platform on Earth. Many of the world&#39;s materials could be made more sustainably through fermentation and renewable feedstocks. However biology is so complex that today, engineering cells to make materials is closer to trial-and-error rather than predictive design. Too many bio-made materials die in the &quot;Valley of Death” gap between a successful experiment in a lab and large-scale commercial fermentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At A-Life, we’re building the AI toolkit to bridge that gap. We specialize in the &quot;cells that make things,&quot; creating the software that allows scientists to engineer biology for real-world performance at scale. We’re building for a bio-economy at scale that’s good for people and the planet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Executive Business Partner, you are at the heart of your team&#39;s operations, anticipating the needs of executives and team members. You resolve operational and administrative issues proactively, ensuring the team stays focused on strategic projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moving quickly within a changing environment, you are flexible and proactive in ambiguous situations. You leverage your knowledge of tools and processes to strategically support team projects. Beyond organization and analytical skills, you possess strong judgment and communication, essential for interacting with diverse stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You take on challenging and meaningful tasks, approaching problems from new angles and constantly asking “what if?” We work together to make the impossible possible, and you are vital to achieving our goals and fostering our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10x impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the administrative landscape (calendars, travel, facilities, equipment) to free executives for strategic priorities. Your attention to detail, combined with a grasp of the big picture, ensures the executive team is always prepared, as well as productive internal problem-solving sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; You act as a confidante and partner to our leadership staff by ensuring their time is spent on the most leveraged activities. You coordinate meetings and clear conflicts for our senior leadership team, and ensure critical meetings aren’t missed or delayed and are prioritized accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a central force within the team, optimizing processes, streamlining workflows, and fostering seamless cross-functional collaboration to fuel rapid growth and scalability. Innovate and elevate by challenging the status quo, building efficiency into existing operations, and shaping new strategies to stay ahead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations &amp;amp; Facilities:&lt;/strong&gt; Managing relationships with landlords and vendors, ordering office supplies, keeping the kitchen stocked, coordinating repairs, and ensuring the physical (or virtual) workspace is safe, clean, and organized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administrative Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Handle core administration, including mail distribution, visitor greeting, and central phone line management, while optimizing company calendars and shared meeting spaces.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture &amp;amp; HR Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Champion internal communications, organize engaging All Hands meetings and offsites, plan memorable events. Partner with HR on onboarding, managing new hire desk setups, tech provisioning, and security badges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct executive support experience, including managing program duties and office management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management, planning, and prioritization skills, with the ability to multitask and adapt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with government agencies, country-level organizations, and C-suite executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth startup, fast-paced org, or similar environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It would be great if you also had these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in supporting executives, including intricate calendar management and consistently maintaining a professional demeanor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with diverse individuals and job functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A balanced approach to problem-solving, applying past expertise while also seeking new answers and learning new tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in establishing new processes, streamlining ineffective programs, and rallying teams around new ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to continuous learning, actively seeking feedback, and fostering a culture of innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in transforming a blank space into a fully functional and organized headquarters to support daily operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for entrepreneurial teams, resourceful problem-solving, bringing joy to the workplace, and contributing to a better world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $118,000 - $176,000 + bonus + benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tapestry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tapestry is a group within Google working to build the AI-powered electric grid. We are tackling one of the world’s most important infrastructure challenges: helping the energy system become more visible, understandable, reliable, affordable, abundant, and clean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Originally born at X, Alphabet’s moonshot factory, Tapestry brings together experts in energy, AI, software engineering, and products to build tools that help the electricity ecosystem plan smarter, move faster, and operate more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global effort. Tapestry supports partners across the U.S., U.K., Chile, New Zealand, Australia, and Brazil as they work toward a cleaner, more resilient energy future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Tapestry means doing high-impact work with a multidisciplinary team tackling a problem that matters at global scale. Learn more about our team and our mission here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Brand &amp;amp; Communications, you will shape Tapestry&#39;s voice, narrative, and reputation as we build a new technology category at the intersection of AI and the electric grid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the CEO as a strategic thought-partner, you will lead our brand and communications strategy across a diverse set of audiences, including utility and enterprise customers, policymakers and industry leaders, employees, Alphabet stakeholders, investors, and the broader public.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with leaders across Product, Engineering, Commercial, and Policy to turn complex technical ideas into clear, credible, and compelling stories. This is a highly strategic, hands-on role for a player-coach who can move seamlessly between advising executives, shaping company positioning, and personally doing the writing and storytelling required to bring that strategy to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You Will Make 10X Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and strengthen Tapestry&#39;s narrative and positioning as we establish a new category at the intersection of AI, software, and the electric grid.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Tapestry&#39;s reputation, influence, and credibility as a trusted industry authority directly and efficiently, leveraging modern communication channels rather than reflexively hiring a large agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand how ideas and information travel today. Design and execute modern communication strategies that span social platforms, creator networks, podcasts, newsletters, niche communities, and executive voice, alongside traditional media relations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technology into compelling stories by partnering with Product, Engineering, and Commercial teams to make sophisticated technical concepts clear, credible, and relevant to customers and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic thought-partner and communications advisor to the CEO and leadership team, shaping executive positioning, thought leadership, key company narratives, and communications during high-impact moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen Tapestry&#39;s connection with employees by building clear internal communication rhythms that connect teams to our mission, strategy, priorities, and progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead corporate and stakeholder communications, partnering with Alphabet and company leadership to clearly articulate Tapestry&#39;s progress, strategy, differentiation, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect and strengthen Tapestry&#39;s reputation by developing thoughtful communications strategies for complex issues involving technology, data privacy, security, regulation, and other high-stakes matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Should Have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Intellectual Agility &amp;amp; Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to quickly develop fluency in complex technical or unfamiliar domains and translate that understanding into effective communications strategy. Prior fluency in grid technology or deep energy expertise is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startup or Founder-Led Success:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated success in startup, entrepreneurial, or founder-led environments, with a proven track record of translating complex technical narratives to broader audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern Media Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; A deep understanding of how ideas move in the modern ecosystem, with practical experience engaging audiences via social, creators, podcasts, newsletters, communities, and executive platforms, not just traditional press.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Player-Coach Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to operate as a strategic advisor to senior executives while remaining hands-on in developing messaging, content, and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional Writing &amp;amp; Storytelling:&lt;/strong&gt; A high bar for clarity, accuracy, and credibility, with the ability to turn complex technical details into a compelling story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Advisory Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated success serving as a trusted advisor to a CEO or senior executive team, particularly in positioning them for high-stakes moments and navigating complex communications challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Resourceful &amp;amp; Agency-Light Approach:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to build broad influence and credibility organically and creatively, without immediately relying on large, expensive agency support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It&#39;d Be Great If You Also Had&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in or exposure to deep tech, enterprise software, AI, or other highly technical domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or repositioning an emerging technology category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with public-sector stakeholders, policy, or regulatory communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tapestry Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take charge:&lt;/strong&gt; We take initiative and own outcomes that move the mission forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transform with purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; We build solutions that solve real problems and create meaningful impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Tapestry, not a thread:&lt;/strong&gt; We collaborate across diverse skills and perspectives to achieve more than we can individually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always fine-tune:&lt;/strong&gt; We stay curious, seek feedback, and refine our understanding as we learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay grounded:&lt;/strong&gt; We listen openly, value different perspectives, and stay focused on what matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A culture that supports growth, ownership, and meaningful impact, along with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and flexible hybrid work model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development&lt;/li&gt;
