&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;he US base salary range for this full-time position is $202,000 - $250,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location. &amp;nbsp;Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, or benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is Alphabet’s moonshot factory where uncomfortably ambitious, world-changing ideas are developed and taken out into the world. X projects have the potential to transform the lives of billions of people and make the world a radically better place. For X to be successful, we have to repeatedly turn breakthrough technology ideas into products that solve large problems in the world, and create meaningful businesses for Alphabet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X’s central Applied AI team is looking for a leader motivated by a desire to make a difference in the world. You will apply your expertise to diverse X projects, tackling domain-specific problems with cutting-edge AI.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Head of the Applied AI team, your work is to discover, invent, solve, and prototype. From devising experiments and building robust implementations to designing new algorithms, You’ll lead a small team of Research Scientists and work on applying artificial intelligence to critically important, often ambiguous, problems. Our team values individuals who can bridge the gap between innovative research and practical, impactful solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10x impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attract and develop a diverse team of ML/AI experts, as well as guide and coach them on all aspects of their research. Foster a collaborative environment for brainstorming, advising, and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner on the technical vision and strategy for our different early stage and early investigation projects; co-design and co-lead a technical roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and deploy robust, scalable ML/AI solutions for real-world problems across multiple X projects and scientific domains, utilizing state of the art developments and techniques with a focus on foundation models and transformer architectures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build hybrid AI models, potentially integrating LLMs with other tools and techniques (e.g., graph-based ML, reinforcement learning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide research and engineering leadership on X early explorations: defining problem scope, identifying optimal AI/ML approaches, and evaluating their merits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide data strategy and contribute to ML pipeline development and system evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to code reviews, establish best practices for ML engineering, and optimize code for performance and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and guide other team members, act as X’s link to the broader research and academic community, as well as to Alphabet’s other research groups, staying abreast of and integrating the latest advancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team of research scientists and in mentoring and guiding junior researchers or engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in&amp;nbsp; applying ML/AI techniques to complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, hands-on experience with LLMs/Transformers, including their theoretical underpinnings and practical application in post-training (e.g., fine-tuning, RLHF,&amp;nbsp; prompting, agent development).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience deploying backend LLM applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and deep experience with ML/Deep Learning frameworks (e.g., TensorFlow, PyTorch, JAX, HuggingFace, LangChain).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with graph-based machine learning techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful experience or a strong understanding of applying AI/ML in another scientific discipline such as biology, psychology, neuroscience, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable research experience, evidenced by contributions to projects, and ideally through publications in relevant ML/NLP venues (e.g., NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, ACL, EMNLP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in a startup or fast-paced R&amp;amp;D environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $307,000 - $422,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About X: &lt;/strong&gt;X is Alphabet’s moonshot factory with a mission of inventing and launching moonshot technologies that could someday make the world a radically better place. We are a diverse group of inventors and entrepreneurs who build and launch technologies that aim to improve the lives of millions, even billions, of people. Our goal: 10x impact on the world’s most intractable problems, not just 10% improvement. We approach projects that have the aspiration and riskiness of research with the speed and ambition of a startup. As an innovation engine, X focuses on repeatedly turning breakthrough-technology ideas into the foundations for large, sustainable businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; In this role, you will sit within the Legal team but embed deeply with X’s Early Pipeline teams. As the primary technical-legal liaison, you will be the connective tissue between these two world-class organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The X Legal team works on the most exciting legal issues since our moonshots require creative and proactive guidance. We challenge ourselves to think big and differently in providing solutions and strategies for our clients—at X, the legal team can be audacious too! Our team aims to accelerate X while demonstrating values of respect, wellbeing, creativity, integrity, and continued development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X’s Early Pipeline team has one goal: creating and incubating X’s next moonshots. They are a dynamic team of creative and collaborative engineers, innovative entrepreneurs, and scientists that focuses on identifying and de-risking ideas. They develop the foundations upon which groundbreaking products and businesses are built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt; X is looking for a deeply curious, technically versatile, and highly strategic IP &amp;amp; Innovation Technical Specialist to accelerate our earliest-stage breakthrough technologies. This role acts as the ultimate bridge between legal strategy and engineering reality. Working hand-in-hand with our Senior IP Counsel and the Early Pipeline teams, you will live at the frontier of innovation—evaluating early moonshot pitches, uncovering uncharted technological &quot;white space,&quot; and mapping out leapfrog opportunities often before a single line of code is written or a prototype is built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will help create and implement unique and innovative IP strategies for X’s exciting &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.company/projects/&quot;&gt;new businesses and technologies&lt;/a&gt;. The IP portfolios you help develop will have a scope stemming from the innovations X produces and a value extending far beyond the immediate products and services X launches. Your contributions here will be a key part of demonstrating a return on investment for these projects. This role is distinct from standard IP roles because it focuses on “de-risking” radical technologies that don’t yet have a defined market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional, back-office patent prosecution role. It is a highly collaborative, high-velocity position designed for a registered patent professional who wants to step directly into the engine room of a moonshot factory. You will use your deep technical acumen and patent expertise to de-risk radical concepts, shape the foundational boundaries of new projects, and translate raw engineering breakthroughs into robust, high-value patent pipelines that protect X’s long-term future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10X impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early Pipeline De-Risking &amp;amp; Shape-Shifting: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner directly with Early Pipeline teams to assess the viability of incoming moonshot pitches. Dig deep into enabling concepts during the conception and maturing phases to actively help teams define project scope and technical parameters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patent-Informed Innovation Harvesting:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead regular brainstorming and high-touch IP harvesting sessions across early and mature project teams. Actively translate core engineering innovations into clear technical differentiators, streamlining raw ideas into a well-defined, value-add patent pipeline aligned with product roadmaps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced IP Landscaping &amp;amp; Market Signals:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead, perform, and direct IP landscaping and white space analysis to identify strategic focus areas for moonshots using patents, non-patent literature, and public discourse. Use these findings and market signals to guide project leads and the IP Counsel on critical decisions regarding market entry or asset transfer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic IP Portfolio Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the IP Counsel in the design and execution of a global IP strategy that aligns with the specific commercial goals of a project. Review and analyze internal and external patent assets to assess scope, perform gap-filling exercises, and help build a competitive “moat” around a project&#39;s core technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Legal-to-Engineering Bridge:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a proactive, high-credibility liaison between engineering, product, and legal teams. Demystify the IP process by instituting regular patent roundtables and delivering technology-led IP trainings, empowering X’s technologists to capture high-quality, robust inventions early.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foundational Asset Creation:&lt;/strong&gt; Synthesize highly complex, early-stage technical concepts into formal Invention Disclosure Forms (IDFs). Manage the initial lifecycle of these disclosures, assist inventors with prioritization, and partner closely with Outside Counsel to drive high-quality external drafting and prosecution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Actionable Freedom to Operate (FTO) Screening:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct initial technical clearings, prior art analysis, and landscape screenings to provide foundational data for FTO risk assessments in cutting-edge, often undefined or uncharted technology spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next-Gen IP Tooling &amp;amp; AI Prototyping:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with core software teams to develop and test cutting-edge, AI-led Moonshot discovery software. Build prompt repositories and standard operating procedures (SOPs) for subject-matter-expert-led white space identification to extract latent value from existing and pending IP assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Technical undergraduate degree in a rigorous engineering or scientific discipline (e.g., Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Physics, Aerospace, Life Sciences, or Materials Science).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;USPTO Registration: &lt;/strong&gt;Admitted to practice before the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office as a Patent Agent or Patent Attorney, with an active USPTO registration number.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;5+ years of experience in patent preparation, prosecution, and IP landscaping, ideally gained within a top-tier law firm technical specialist/patent agent program or a high-growth deep-tech corporate environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early Portfolio Lifecycle Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience building, scaling, and managing patent portfolios for early-stage deep tech startups, university tech-transfer offices, or novel corporate R&amp;amp;D spin-outs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Chameleon:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional, broad technical literacy with the ability to rapidly pivot between a wide range of technical domains and assess IP potential across diverse technological frontiers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elite Communication &amp;amp; Translation Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to go toe-to-toe with PhD-level researchers and world-class engineers, extract their core technical breakthroughs, and seamlessly translate them into actionable IP strategies while maintaining strong cross-functional relationships.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ambiguity Champion:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on ability to make structured decisions with incomplete information and thrive with high levels of autonomy in a fast-paced, &quot;fail-fast&quot; scrappy start up environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tech-Forward Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability and enthusiasm to leverage cutting-edge developments in AI and generative prompting to enable smarter, more efficient work processes and white space discovery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It would be great if you also had these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Patent Analytics Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep familiarity with modern patent analytics platforms (e.g., IPFolio, PatSnap, Anaqua, LexisNexis TotalPatent) and a strong enthusiasm for leveraging generative AI to automate white-space analysis and prompt engineering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Tech Specialization:&lt;/strong&gt; A solid technical understanding of artificial intelligence, robotics, physics, clean energy, biotechnology, bioinformatics, or related deep-tech domains.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startup Agility:&lt;/strong&gt; A gritty, startup-oriented &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mindset—someone who is equally excited about defining high-level competitive landscapes as they are about digging into the fine details of a technical disclosure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience effectively presenting complex technological landscapes and IP insights to senior management, business executives, and cross-functional technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $184,000 - $273,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team – &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.company/projects/bellwether/&quot;&gt;Bellwether&lt;/a&gt; – operates at the intersection of machine learning, geospatial data, and pressing issues with enterprise customers, governments, and more. Our team is focused on creating transparency into physical risk. We focus on severe weather manifestations of climate change, such as wildfires, and aim to use a wide range of data and analytics to better understand and predict what these events could mean for communities and businesses across the globe. We do this through the detection and classification of the features and patterns of the natural and built worlds, the application of cutting-edge machine learning, and the redesign of the full geo-ML workflow. This work extends into development and production-level work as well, as Bellwether also has a number of products that are live with customers. The result: tools and models that allow a range of industries to better leverage earth observation insights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Product Manager at Bellwether, you will drive the evolution of our core product suite and take complete ownership of all model, agent, and platform components for Bellwether. In this highly technical role, you will help shape how financial services and government customers leverage AI. You will work closely with internal users and customers to prioritize their complex requirements and ship valuable features / workflows to the Bellwether platform. You will collaborate deeply with the engineering, research, and cross-functional teams to ensure our agent architecture and data infrastructure remain ahead of model capabilities, establishing Bellwether as the most robust and intelligent platform in the space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As model intelligence accelerates, the ultimate form factor of agentic systems and scalable data platforms remains unwritten. We seek a highly technical product leader who combines deep architectural understanding, a genuine passion for platform engineering, and strong product intuition. You should be equally comfortable discussing advanced agent behaviors and data pipelines with world-class researchers, debugging user workflows, and presenting product strategy to executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will have 10X impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain clear, inspiring product vision, roadmaps, segmentation, and value proposition across our key verticals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong point of view on how agentic system, data ontology and enterprise AI models are evolving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deep-dive discovery with key stakeholders in the insurance, capital markets, and resilience sectors to turn complex climate modeling into intuitive risk measurement and mitigation workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create experiences that inspire confidence, delight and accelerate our end users, and encourage adoption and trust across industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with our researchers, engineers, designers, and partners to guide development and bring our roadmap to life during the product lifecycle:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the market, our partners, and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain focus on roadmap priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and scope sprints and releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose creative solutions to technical issues and challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear, concise product documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create materials and give presentations that evangelize and articulate product vision, roadmap, and value propositions to technical and non-technical audiences, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand and monitor the market and ecosystem for physical risk - including insurance, reinsurance, capital markets, and more&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combined 10+ years of professional experience spanning product management and engineering, including at least 1 year in a hands-on engineering role. Ideally, you transitioned from a highly technical discipline (e.g., Software Engineering, Computer Science, or Data Science) early in your career, or you bring entrepreneurial founder experience or product leadership that culminated in a successful company acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of success in platform or enterprise product management. You have demonstrated tangible, measurable business results utilizing either a product-led (PLG) or sales-led (SLG) growth strategy (or a hybrid of both).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep domain expertise in cloud infrastructure and platform architecture (familiarity with technologies like Databricks, CoreWeave, Splunk, Snowflake, etc., is highly valued). Candidates with consumer-product backgrounds are encouraged to apply, provided you directly own the underlying core platform or infrastructure components.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience utilizing Generative AI tools to optimize product workflows, accelerate PRD development, enhance Product-to-Engineering alignment, and rapidly prototype wireframes or feature concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deeply technical mindset coupled with the ability to navigate a highly cross-functional environment, seamlessly bridging complex engineering architectures with executive business strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in startups or small-team environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Google’s AI tools and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with geospatial data (e.g., satellite imagery, GIS), climate science, or catastrophe modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Google Cloud and enterprise deployments Prior success in productizing research or innovation-stage prototypes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing samples or public-facing documentation that demonstrate clarity and technical fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $240,000 - $338,000 + bonus + benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About X, the Moonshot Factory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is a diverse group of inventors and entrepreneurs who build and launch technologies that aim to improve the lives of millions, even billions, of people. Our goal: 10x impact on the world’s most intractable problems, not just 10% improvement. We approach projects that have the aspiration and riskiness of research with the speed and ambition of a startup.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team –&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.company/projects/bellwether/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bellwether&lt;/a&gt; – operates at the intersection of machine learning, geospatial data, and pressing issues with enterprise customers, governments, and more. We focus on severe weather manifestations of climate change, such as wildfires, and aim to use a wide range of data and analytics to better understand and predict what these events could mean for communities and businesses across the globe. We do this through the detection and classification of the features and patterns of the natural and built worlds, the application of cutting-edge machine learning, and the redesign of the full geo-ML workflow. This work extends into development and production-level work as well, as Bellwether also has a number of products that are live with customers. The result: tools and models that allow a range of industries to better leverage earth observation insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a hands-on Machine Learning Lead engineer, contributing to all aspects of the project’s development and deployment of applications. We are looking for a motivated expert level ML Engineer with broad experience across systems architecture and design in one or more cloud platforms. This role would guide machine learning for Bellwether’s real-world products, and is not a research-based role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is small but mighty and highly collaborative, and values pair programming and cooperative ideation. We are committed to agile principles and rely heavily on this framework for efficient sprints and cycles. We are looking for passionate and driven people, who are comfortable moving between creative, big-picture thinking and specifics of how to execute. We operate in a fast-paced, fluid environment as our team moves from early stage development into production phases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10x impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embracing your ability to be a ML ‘expert generalist’, enjoying the fluidity of moving from architecting new production systems, to machine learning, to security and monitoring. From high level strategy to specific tactics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive and execute key decisions on software architecture and features, balancing business needs&amp;nbsp; and our technology roadmap, balancing longevity with rapid prototyping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute as a key team member to the creation of new systems and processes to ensure high quality development, deployment, and maintenance of live applications in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain Google Cloud Platform-based infrastructure for software development and high-volume production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present findings to team members, internal and external stakeholders, and help set a direction for future development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree or PhD in Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, Physics, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
