&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: This role was previously titled &#39;Firestarter&#39;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Evergreen Position&lt;/strong&gt;. We are continuously accepting applications to build a pipeline of talented individuals for the future. While we may not have an immediate vacancy, we review applications periodically and will reach out as specific needs arise throughout the year. Please expect a delay in response after submitting your application.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is Alphabet’s moonshot factory with a mission of inventing and launching “moonshot” technologies that could someday make the world a radically better place. We are a diverse group of inventors and entrepreneurs who build and launch technologies that aim to improve the lives of millions, even billions, of people. Our goal: 10x impact on the world’s most intractable problems, not just 10% improvement. We approach projects that have the aspiration and riskiness of research with the speed and ambition of a startup. As an innovation engine, X focuses on repeatedly turning breakthrough-technology ideas into the foundations for large, sustainable businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking leaders and entrepreneurs who are motivated by a passion to change the world for the better. In this role you will have access to resources including X and Alphabet’s extensive network and convening abilities, state-of-the-art prototyping facilities and laboratories, proprietary tools, ‘&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.company/blog/posts/moonshot-compost/&quot;&gt;moonshot compost&lt;/a&gt;’, world-class technical and business expert collaborators, and unique innovation processes to help you explore and develop breakthrough technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will align with our earliest existing investigations and have the ability to develop ideas from inception at X.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10x impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a combination of critical thinking, networking, research, and prototyping to propose and assess potential breakthrough technology-enabled projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Xers to develop moonshot ideas. Progressively de-risk ideas both from technical and business perspectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and refine your moonshot story and pitch as your advancements are made&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage resources at X and Alphabet in your pursuit of creating moonshots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 years experience as a leader or entrepreneur in a technical industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience playing a key role in successfully taking new tech from idea inception to product launch, in particular deep tech, while working in a startup environment. You are biased to action and will “roll up your sleeves”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to create external partnerships around early-stage technology&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build an A+ team. You have a track record in spotting, attracting and retaining top talent across functions and levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in ambiguity and able to manage your own work with tenacity and a sense of urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had these:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to de-risk a new product idea from both the technical and business perspectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to effectively communicate both technical and non-technical information to mixed audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by purpose and passion; you fall in love with problems, not solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $221,000 - $328,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tapestry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tapestry is a group within Google working to build the AI-powered electric grid. We are tackling one of the world’s most important infrastructure challenges: helping the energy system become more visible, understandable, reliable, affordable, abundant, and clean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Originally born at X, Alphabet’s moonshot factory, Tapestry brings together experts in energy, AI, software engineering, and products to build tools that help the electricity ecosystem plan smarter, move faster, and operate more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global effort. Tapestry supports partners across the U.S., U.K., Chile, New Zealand, Australia, and Brazil as they work toward a cleaner, more resilient energy future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Tapestry means doing high-impact work with a multidisciplinary team tackling a problem that matters at global scale. Learn more about our team and our mission&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tapestryenergy.com/en&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead advanced research and development efforts focused on improving the stability, resilience, and controllability of the electric grid through next-generation utility-scale inverter control. Your work will center on designing, simulating, and validating novel control and orchestration algorithms for inverter-based resources operating under a wide range of grid conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary objective will be to expand Tapestry’s control and orchestration capabilities by developing advanced inverter control strategies that address critical challenges such as mode shifting, automatic gain control, and stable operation across strong and weak grid environments. You will work from concept through implementation, contributing both theoretical insight and practical simulation artifacts that inform future product development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, six-month PhD residency designed for candidates conducting doctoral research in power electronics, power systems, or advanced control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10X Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop advanced control algorithms for utility-scale inverter systems focused on grid stability and resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and validate mode-shifting inverter control strategies that enable seamless transitions between operating modes, such as grid-following (GFL) and grid-forming (GFM) for both single and three phase inverters.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement Automatic Gain Control (AGC) approaches that dynamically adapt inverter behavior based on real-time grid conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simulate and evaluate control strategies under a range of operating conditions, including strong grid, weak grid, and transient scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate advanced control concepts into implementation-ready algorithms suitable for future firmware or hardware integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with power systems, software, and product teams to align research outcomes with real-world grid applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear technical documentation outlining control design, assumptions, performance tradeoffs, and stability margins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in a PhD program in Electrical Engineering, Power Electronics, Power Systems, Control Systems, or a closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundational knowledge of power electronics and utility-scale power systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with grid-forming, grid-following, or microgrid control strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with the Texas Instruments (TI) Digital Signal Processor (DSP) i.e C2000 and relevant software tools i.e Code Composer Studio(CCS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or analyzing control systems for inverter-based resources i.e inverter firmware development using interrupts etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with simulation tools such as MATLAB/Simulink, PLECS, and/or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to reason about system stability and dynamic behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills for technical documentation and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had one or more of&amp;nbsp; these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with grid-forming, grid-following, or microgrid control strategies implementation using hierarchical control.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with wide-bandgap (WBG) devices and inverter hardware considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to firmware or hardware-software interface constraints for power electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating academic research into applied or industry-focused outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in grid modernization, renewable integration, and decarbonization of the electric power system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take charge&lt;/strong&gt;: We take initiative and own outcomes that move the mission forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transform with purpose: &lt;/strong&gt;We build solutions that solve real problems and create meaningful impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Tapestry, not a thread&lt;/strong&gt;: We collaborate across diverse skills and perspectives to achieve more than we can individually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always fine-tune&lt;/strong&gt;: We stay curious, seek feedback, and refine our understanding as we learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay grounded&lt;/strong&gt;: We listen openly, value different perspectives, and stay focused on what matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A culture that supports growth, ownership, and meaningful impact, along with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Immersion in a world-class research environment at the intersection of AI and climate tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive residency stipend and housing relocation support for the duration of the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct mentorship from industry-leading research scientists and engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on &quot;moonshot&quot; problems with access to Alphabet-scale compute and resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this position is $109,000 - $150,000 + benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include benefits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tapestry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tapestry is a group within Google working to build the AI-powered electric grid. We are tackling one of the world’s most important infrastructure challenges: helping the energy system become more visible, understandable, reliable, affordable, abundant, and clean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Originally born at X, Alphabet’s moonshot factory, Tapestry brings together experts in energy, AI, software engineering, and products to build tools that help the electricity ecosystem plan smarter, move faster, and operate more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global effort. Tapestry supports partners across the U.S., U.K., Chile, New Zealand, Australia, and Brazil as they work toward a cleaner, more resilient energy future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining Tapestry means doing high-impact work with a multidisciplinary team tackling a problem that matters at global scale. Learn more about our team and our mission &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tapestryenergy.com/en&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will serve as a strategic technical bridge across cross-functional engineering, product, and partner teams to shape and execute Tapestry’s end-to-end grid model strategy. You will lead efforts to transform complex, multi-source industry grid and network data into unified, high-quality standards, such as the Common Information Model (CIM). By driving model quality assurance, optimizing data ingestion, and continuously refining our validation frameworks, you will play a pivotal role in scaling the reach, reliability, and real-world impact of our AI-powered grid platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10X Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Technical Bridge: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as the primary technical liaison connecting internal and external cross functional teams to align on data requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Co-pilot to Product Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the domain knowledge expert to help Product Manager to define the Model Ingestion User Journey and Functional Requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ingestion Execution and Tooling Feedback: &lt;/strong&gt;Utilize internal ingestion tooling to process and convert grid models from industry comment file format into CIM format. Actively collaborate with Software Engineering to provide operational feedback, flag bugs, and drive improvements for future tooling automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model Quality Assurance: &lt;/strong&gt;Validate that all ingested models meet explicit use-case requirements with specified technical data requirements. This includes running iterative checks to ensure models are correctly geolocated and electrically simulatable with acceptable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Deployment: &lt;/strong&gt;Stage and deliver validated grid models into target testing and production applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead User Acceptance Testing: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct rigorous application-level testing of the models to verify performance, coordinate with end-users for validation, and provide final engineering sign-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Masters degree in Electrical Engineering, Power Systems or related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in power systems modeling and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical understanding of power system topologies and explicit experience working with Common Information Model (CIM) standard and data conversion between CIM and other commonly used data formats in the power industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and oversee the structural CIM implementation strategy, ensuring accurate representation of complex grid equipment, steady-state hypotheses, and dynamic topologies across multi-vendor utility datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognized contributions to or participation in CIM user groups (e.g., CIMug / UCA International Users Group), IEC Technical Committee 57 (IEC TC57) working groups (specifically those managing IEC 61970 and 61968), or open-source CIM tooling communities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of power system principles, including power flow, short circuit analysis, transient stability, and economic dispatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in power system analysis software and experience working with physical grid data (GIS) and operational datasets&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience/knowledge&amp;nbsp; in scientific programming languages (e.g, Matlab, Python, JAX, C++, Julia, etc.) with a desire to expand into new areas of coding languages and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort navigating modern software environments, interacting with data layers, using ingestion tools, and collaborating closely with developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had one or more of these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ph.D (or equivalent experience) in Electrical Engineering, Power Systems or related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with open-source power systems tools, libraries, or data repositories is a plus but not strictly required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering scalable solutions to complex software problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in startup or high-growth environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tapestry Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take charge:&lt;/strong&gt; We take initiative and own outcomes that move the mission forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transform with purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; We build solutions that solve real problems and create meaningful impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Tapestry, not a thread: &lt;/strong&gt;We collaborate across diverse skills and perspectives to achieve more than we can individually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always fine-tune:&lt;/strong&gt; We stay curious, seek feedback, and refine our understanding as we learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay grounded:&lt;/strong&gt; We listen openly, value different perspectives, and stay focused on what matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following areas are handled by cross-functional partners:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Software &amp;amp; Automation Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Use and provide feedback on the tools, and not responsible for writing production code to build the underlying platform or automate the pipeline infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Upstream Data Sourcing &amp;amp; Commercial Relations: &lt;/strong&gt;Managing the initial commercial relationship with utilities or navigating the legalities of data sharing remains with the Partnerships and Data Science team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A culture that supports growth, ownership, and meaningful impact, along with…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and flexible hybrid work model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work on important real-world problems within an Alphabet-backed environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this position is $159,000 - $277,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
