&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking a Cloud Operations Engineer to lead technical vision and implementation of internal and multi-customer cloud infrastructure. In this role you will have the opportunity to drive architecture decisions that bridge teams across platform engineering, cloud operations, and product delivery. You will also support internal developer experience by automating operations such as CI, scaling analysis workflows, and ensure our cloud infrastructure maintains enterprise grade security, reliability, and cost management.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your technical vision will extend beyond the near-term sprint contributions. It will guide long-term multi-year roadmaps, mentor and establish standards across the engineering teams, and champion operating procedures to proactively manage incident responses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will have 10X impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, deploy, and manage scalable, high-throughput, low-latency, and multi-region cloud infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead structural initiatives across cloud providers, focusing on microservices, serverless patterns, and zero-trust security controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain self-service Internal Developer Platform (IDP) that allow software engineering teams to provision, test, and ship code securely and autonomously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Streamline CI/CD pipeline capabilities, reducing build-to-deploy cycle times while enforcing compliance, guardrails, and security scanning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eliminate team friction through advanced orchestration, custom cloud operators, and robust automation tooling..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion end-to-end system visibility by designing unified observability frameworks incorporating metrics, logs, distributed tracing, and continuous profiling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement robust Service Level Indicators (SLIs), Service Level Objectives (SLOs), and Error Budgets across core microservices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an escalation authority for critical production incidents, driving root-cause analysis (RCA) and blameless post-mortem actions to eliminate repeat failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish continuously monitored FinOps practices—driving visibility into cloud spending, workload unit economics, capacity planning, right-sizing, and committed use reservation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and enforce automated right-sizing, lifecycle policies, committed use/reservation strategies, and continuous cost optimization patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering leaders to establish resource allocation models and cost attribution tags without compromising performance or speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
