&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a highly motivated and experienced engineering leader to join our growing team. In this role, you will own and lead the technical strategy and development for enterprise applications that will meet the needs of an evolving electric grid at planet scale. You will be a standard-bearer for engineering excellence and establish the tools, architecture, and best practices that empower our teams. You will lead teams through ambiguous and complex charters, driving innovation and pushing the boundaries of what&#39;s possible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will make 10X Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and drive Technical Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and drive a forward-looking technical vision that closely aligns with product roadmaps and customer priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect at Scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide the architecture and design of enterprise applications with the right emphasis on future scale, complexity, availability, fault tolerance, and security to earn partner trust and meet Google-scale reliability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional collaboration and leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner seamlessly with product managers, user experience designers, data scientists, power systems engineers, and other engineering leaders to deliver high-impact solutions. You will translate high-level business ambiguity into concrete technical roadmaps for your teams and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on technical contributions:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain strong technical depth and provide technical guidance and mentorship to the team on design and implementation, diving deep as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and develop high-performing teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Coach and develop engineers and technical leaders, foster a strong engineering culture, and build the organizational capabilities needed to deliver against Tapestry&#39;s long-term goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 12+ years of experience in software engineering with a deep focus on distributed systems, backend infrastructure, and enterprise applications, with at least 10 years in formal people management or high-impact technical leadership roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architectural Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of designing, building, and scaling reliable production systems and applications. Thorough knowledge of large-scale data processing and modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of reliability engineering, performance optimization, and establishing engineering tools and processes for large teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; The ability to translate high-level &quot;moonshot&quot; ambiguity into concrete technical roadmaps for your team and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD in Computer Science or a related quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a &quot;zero-to-one&quot; environment or building out a new geographic engineering site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building LLM-orchestrated distributed systems or autonomous agent frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for using data and technology to create a future with reliable, affordable, and clean energy for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take charge:&lt;/strong&gt; We take initiative and own outcomes that move the mission forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transform with purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; We build solutions that solve real problems and create meaningful impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Tapestry, not a thread: &lt;/strong&gt;We collaborate across diverse skills and perspectives to achieve more than we can individually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always fine-tune:&lt;/strong&gt; We stay curious, seek feedback, and refine our understanding as we learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay grounded:&lt;/strong&gt; We listen openly, value different perspectives, and stay focused on what matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A culture that supports growth, ownership, and meaningful impact, along with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and flexible hybrid work model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work on important real-world problems within an Alphabet-backed environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $262,000 - $369,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is Alphabet’s moonshot factory. We are a diverse group of inventors and entrepreneurs who build and launch technologies that aim to improve the lives of millions, even billions, of people. Our goal: 10x impact on the world’s most intractable problems, not just 10% improvement. We approach projects that have the aspiration and riskiness of research with the speed and ambition of a startup.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re X’s moonshot for the global supply chain, applying AI to reduce waste, fragility, and inefficiency. We’re an agile team of experienced AI researchers, software engineers, and entrepreneurs working with visionary partners and customers around the world to make sure everyone has sustainable and reliable access to the food, medicine, clothing, and other goods and services they need.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people who are passionate about revolutionizing the global supply chain to join us at this critical growth stage. You’ll be part of a fast-paced team that has the agility and impact of an early stage company, while building on world-class Google AI technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer, you will drive the on-the-ground implementation of our Enterprise AI products to completely reimagine the global supply chain. This is a highly customer-facing, builder-first role that demands a rigorous balance of strategic client partnership, and tactical, hands-on execution—writing code to develop customer-specific product extensions, build tailored solutions for unique user needs, develop robust customer data ingestion pipelines, and architect seamless integrations. Sitting shoulder-to-shoulder with daily end-users and enterprise IT, you will drive 10X economic impact by turning messy operational realities into scalable software. Acting as the engineering vanguard on the front lines, you will directly drive core platform evolution based on ground-truth realities, while extensively leveraging AI to de-bottleneck deployments and ensure rapid, frictionless launches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will have 10X impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end technical deployment of our Enterprise AI products, acting as the definitive on-site engineering authority to deliver AI-native capabilities that transform global supply chains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and build technical integrations, connecting or entirely replacing legacy enterprise systems via robust bi-directional data pipelines, APIs, and agent-to-agent communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate complex enterprise IT environments to deploy our AI platform, orchestrating rollouts across diverse cloud, hybrid, and agentic architectures to get our software live and into users&#39; hands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with clients, end-users, and IT on the ground to translate messy operational supply chain realities into concrete engineering tasks and AI-native workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code immediate, customer-specific product adaptations, balancing rapid hands-on execution with active Platform Engineering collaboration to shape core capabilities using field realities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively clear technical, security, and adoption hurdles, extensively leveraging AI alongside client IT teams to debottleneck the deployment process and rapidly accelerate rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Codify field solutions into reusable deployment playbooks and software blocks, bridging high-agency on-site execution with scalable core platform engineering rather than delivering one-off tweaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or equivalent highly technical practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in customer-facing engineering or forward deployed roles, with a proven track record of owning hands-on technical delivery, system integrations, and implementation of AI or sophisticated SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with prompt engineering, building agentic workflows, and wiring up LLMs to external systems (via function calling, APIs, or MCPs) to solve complex reasoning, routing, and automation tasks in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production-grade Python or TypeScript for complex system integration, building bidirectional data pipelines to sync data and systematically strangle messy legacy systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own high-stakes technical deployments from end to end, driving rapid engineering decisions and aligning a variety of stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency in environments with high velocity, ambiguity, and minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’d be great if you also had these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience working within supply chains, procurement, or new product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced technical, business, or SCM degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $197,000 - $285,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.company/projects/circularity/&quot;&gt;Materra&lt;/a&gt; is on a mission to radically reduce global waste and move to a true circular economy. The team has developed technology that identifies waste material at the molecular level—starting with plastics. Materra works with industry partners to improve the way recycling centers process plastics using AI and robotics, to make recycling more affordable and scalable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Machine Learning Data Engineer (DataOps)&lt;/strong&gt; to build and unify the data infrastructure that powers our model training pipelines. In this role, you will lead the effort to consolidate fragmented data sources into a cohesive, high-quality data foundation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your primary focus will be designing automated ingestion pipelines, establishing data quality validation frameworks, and managing dataset versioning to support our machine learning training loops. You will bridge the gap between operations, remote annotation teams, and machine learning engineers to ensure our models are trained on reliable, well-structured data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and build automated ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) and ELT (Extract, Load, Transform) data pipelines to aggregate, clean, and harmonize data from disparate sources, databases, and operational ingestion flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement DataOps practices, including data quality monitoring, automated schema validation, and anomaly detection to catch corrupt or mislabeled data early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize and integrate third-party annotation workflows and remote labeling feeds into unified datasets ready for model training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain dataset versioning and storage systems to allow reproducible machine learning experiments and seamless data retrieval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with machine learning engineers and operations teams to translate raw material, form factor, and sensor metadata into structured training features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in Computer Science, Data Engineering, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Engineering &amp;amp; Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years&amp;nbsp; experience building scalable data pipelines, managing relational and non-relational databases, and unifying fragmented data storage systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern Python Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Expertise in Python and data manipulation libraries (e.g., Pandas, NumPy, or SQL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality &amp;amp; DataOps:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience implementing automated data validation, quality control frameworks, and dataset versioning practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ML Data Lifecycle Understanding:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience structuring datasets specifically for machine learning workflows, including handling annotations, metadata tracking, and training set curation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Google Cloud Ecosystem:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with Google Cloud platform tools (e.g., BigQuery, Cloud Storage, Dataflow, Dataproc, Vertex AI Data Pipelines).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing pipelines using Google Cloud Composer or equivalent orchestration frameworks (e.g., Apache Airflow, Prefect, Dagster).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal / Unstructured Data:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience handling mixed data types, including image datasets, sensor metadata, and unstructured physical property records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Annotation Platform Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with data labeling platforms, human-in-the-loop workflows, or integrating third-party annotation APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Validation &amp;amp; Versioning Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Exposure to data quality and ML versioning tools (e.g., Great Expectations, DVC, or TFX/Data Validation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $164,000 - $261,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;

